Z||000008||MontanaFiero||09-12-2001||12:49 AM||||I think it's around $20, but then there's shipping. Call him @ 1-866-FIEROGT and get yourself on his list. (There, George-- I sent you another customer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>Hey Neal-- <BR>The drill guide is now stuck on some UPS plane at some airport because of some idiot  mother-@#&!%# terrorists. So much for "next-day air".<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||09-12-2001||04:36 PM||||If you use the fiero ECM and induction system, which is designed for a 2.8 僕iter engine than expect to have fuel mixture and spark advance problems. You're going to need a custom prom chip to get it right. You値l need a scan tool too. <P>I speak from experience! <P>  <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfixit58||09-12-2001||04:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>If you use the fiero ECM and induction system, which is designed for a 2.8 僕iter engine than expect to have fuel mixture and spark advance problems. You're going to need a custom prom chip to get it right. You値l need a scan tool too. <P>I speak from experience! <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's the first I've hear this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> I've always read that you can either increase the fuel pressure or install the 3.4 fuel injectors and your good to go. Did you try the above before you had a custom chip made?<P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000011||BC-GT||09-12-2001||08:25 PM||||FWIW, I phoned Ed Parks a couple weeks ago and chatted with him about this stuff. His reply was, use everything from your Fiero, even the 2.8 injectors are worthy, <B>BUT</B>, get an adjustable pressure regulator for the fuel line. BTW, a super nice guy who took the time to answer all my questions even after I told him right off the bat that he was way to far away for me to buy a motor off him.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||09-12-2001||09:46 PM||||It will run rich with the 3.4 injectors in closed loop, which means it will run rich at full throttle or hard acceleration. You won't realize the full power potential of the engine because of this rich condition.  <P>An adjustable fuel pressure regulator is one way to mask the problem; it's a quick fix but in my opinion not the best fix. <P>My 3.4 is modified (flows more air than a stock 3.4) and even my engine runs rich with 40.5 psi of fuel pressure. I can only imagine a stock 3.4 must run richer. I don't even need the cold start injector to fire it up on a cold morning. I also get black smoke from the exhaust when I accelerate hard from a stop.  I have 1150 miles on my new motor and the new Borla exhaust tips look like they have 100,000+ miles on them because of the carbon buildup on them.<P>Last year when I talked to Ed he told me he was using the stock 2.8 injectors on his stock 3.4 motors and turning the fuel pressure up a little.   <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
